WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.421
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.691 --> 00:01.802
(About Ms. Suda…)

3
00:02.170 --> 00:03.197
(Ms. Suda?)

4
00:04.555 --> 00:05.902
(Why did you do this?)

5
00:05.950 --> 00:09.247
The fact that she abandoned your class and refused to continue teaching

6
00:10.016 --> 00:12.016
was a serious dereliction of her duty as a teacher.

7
00:12.340 --> 00:13.798
As student council president,

8
00:14.237 --> 00:15.900
I can’t let this continue.

9
00:18.250 --> 00:19.490
Do you wanna wipe your face?

10
02:06.850 --> 02:07.850
You’ve got everything?

11
02:07.998 --> 02:09.202
I think so, mom.

12
02:09.570 --> 02:11.804
But I saw a toothbrush on the table.

13
02:12.810 --> 02:14.002
That I forgot.

14
02:15.050 --> 02:16.700
Hurry, you’re gonna miss the bus.

15
02:17.234 --> 02:20.167
We’re so early. I don’t think the bus has arrived yet.

16
02:20.207 --> 02:21.503
We have to make sure.

17
02:22.402 --> 02:24.484
I’m just going on a school trip.

18
02:24.506 --> 02:26.797
Why are you guys so excited?

19
02:27.550 --> 02:29.120
Well, you’ve never done this before.

20
02:29.150 --> 02:30.779
Of course, I’m excited.

21
02:33.000 --> 02:34.620
- Let’s go. - See you, Mom.

22
02:34.660 --> 02:37.500
(This is my very first school trip.)

23
02:37.757 --> 02:40.623
(This will be a trip I’ll never forget.)

24
02:40.840 --> 02:41.840
Let’s go, Dad.

25
02:51.170 --> 02:54.296
1…2…3.

26
02:55.518 --> 02:56.820
Okay.

27
02:57.370 --> 02:59.656
If anyone wants to make a donation, there’s a booth over to the side.

28
02:59.680 --> 03:02.285
And those who want to pray can head upstairs.

29
03:02.325 --> 03:04.053
See you on the bus in half an hour.

30
03:04.274 --> 03:05.274
Let’s go.

31
03:05.712 --> 03:06.987
Come on, Ji. Let’s see the elephant.

32
03:07.011 --> 03:08.011
Elephant?

33
03:25.330 --> 03:26.330
I give up.

34
03:27.143 --> 03:28.411
Let’s donate some coins instead.

35
03:28.435 --> 03:29.743
It’s so freaking hot here.

36
03:29.770 --> 03:32.180
No way, Kong. I won’t give up that easy.

37
03:32.797 --> 03:34.600
I should have stayed in my damned room.

38
03:35.700 --> 03:37.200
Language! We’re at a temple.

39
03:37.571 --> 03:38.571
Ugh.

40
03:40.910 --> 03:41.976
We’ll be here all day.

41
03:43.001 --> 03:45.370
The bus is leaving at 10.

42
03:45.400 --> 03:46.697
Why are you guys still here?

43
03:46.970 --> 03:50.004
Ty said he wouldn’t leave until he successfully threw the coin.

44
03:50.420 --> 03:51.622
Class 7.

45
03:52.860 --> 03:54.247
Why aren’t you on the bus yet?

46
03:54.922 --> 03:57.530
And Kongpob, you’re the last person from class 9.

47
03:57.750 --> 04:00.463
Ty won’t leave until he can throw the coin in the elephant’s mouth.

48
04:01.546 --> 04:04.137
Okay, Tyler. I’ll give you one more chance.

49
04:04.390 --> 04:07.297
Okay, I’ll get it this time.

50
04:24.134 --> 04:25.404
See? I did it.

51
04:25.734 --> 04:26.623
How did I do?

52
04:26.642 --> 04:28.198
- Spectacular. - Did I do well, guys?

53
04:28.430 --> 04:29.200
Amazing.

54
04:29.285 --> 04:29.900
Go.

55
04:29.951 --> 04:32.182
Get on the bus. Kongpob, you too.

56
04:32.200 --> 04:32.693
Yes.

57
04:32.711 --> 04:33.711
Come on.

58
04:35.305 --> 04:36.503
Kong, wait for me!

59
04:37.382 --> 04:38.382
Come on, Kong.

60
05:01.309 --> 05:02.949
Why aren’t you guys having fun like them?

61
05:20.973 --> 05:23.245
Want some popsicles?

62
05:23.280 --> 05:24.902
Do you want some popsicles?

63
05:26.640 --> 05:28.004
Here, my brother.

64
05:29.910 --> 05:30.602
Thank you.

65
05:30.777 --> 05:32.297
I guarantee it’s so good.

66
05:33.592 --> 05:34.992
Don’t you wanna take a look around?

67
05:41.454 --> 05:42.494
Wanna go together?

68
05:48.048 --> 05:50.702
Popsicle? Tyler made this himself.

69
05:52.200 --> 05:53.302
Can we get another one?

70
06:07.090 --> 06:08.100
Here, Ji.

71
06:14.582 --> 06:16.502
That was… a bit weird.

72
06:22.680 --> 06:23.970
TRADITIONAL THAI COFFEE

73
06:33.933 --> 06:34.933
You want some?

74
06:36.426 --> 06:40.380
You can sense my thirst coming through my skin?

75
06:41.780 --> 06:42.780
Mmm.

76
06:44.065 --> 06:45.065
Let’s go.

77
06:50.173 --> 06:52.299
- Can I have an iced cocoa? - Of course.

78
06:54.939 --> 06:55.939
I’ll have the same.

79
06:57.020 --> 06:58.097
Make that two, please.

80
06:58.576 --> 06:59.576
Sure.

81
07:01.100 --> 07:03.459
- Here. - Oh, no. I got this.

82
07:04.490 --> 07:05.490
It’s okay.

83
07:17.675 --> 07:18.675
I’ll take…

84
07:26.480 --> 07:29.102
For the cocoa.

85
07:40.130 --> 07:41.250
What’s this, Ji?

86
07:42.127 --> 07:43.598
Looks like a gymnast.

87
07:45.860 --> 07:48.300
That’s a sugar sculpture of a fishing monkey.

88
07:48.524 --> 07:50.000
- Sugar sculpture? - Mmm.

89
07:50.291 --> 07:51.737
So it’s edible?

90
07:51.777 --> 07:52.777
Umm…

91
07:53.075 --> 07:54.228
This is for Ruth.

92
07:54.270 --> 07:56.666
- If you want it… - You can have it. I’m good.

93
07:57.081 --> 07:58.462
Really? I’ll take this one then.

94
08:01.053 --> 08:02.053
Come on, Kong.

95
08:03.380 --> 08:04.380
What?

96
08:04.451 --> 08:05.496
Thank you, Ji.

97
08:11.180 --> 08:13.260
This one’s not bitten. You can take a bite.

98
08:17.312 --> 08:18.312
Hey.

99
08:50.521 --> 08:52.398
Hey, I said just a bite.

100
08:55.854 --> 08:57.201
I said just a bite.

101
08:57.466 --> 08:58.625
You ate the whole thing.

102
08:59.200 --> 09:00.574
Eat it.

103
09:26.878 --> 09:27.900
Doesn’t look like me.

104
09:28.109 --> 09:29.109
It does.

105
09:45.342 --> 09:46.342
That one.

106
09:46.441 --> 09:47.614
- Which one? - The red one.

107
09:50.767 --> 09:52.822
Yes, see how good I am?

108
09:53.050 --> 09:54.050
Thank you.

109
09:54.920 --> 09:55.920
Here.

110
09:56.360 --> 09:57.500
- Huh? - Take it.

111
09:58.010 --> 09:59.666
I’ve won so many of these.

112
10:01.090 --> 10:02.345
So cute. A big one.

113
10:07.592 --> 10:08.847
-Mr. Tin -Huh?

114
10:08.877 --> 10:10.472
Take a picture for us.

115
10:10.502 --> 10:11.340
Oh, wow.

116
10:11.505 --> 10:13.428
Open your eyes. Don’t fear the sun.

117
10:13.450 --> 10:14.602
It’s too bright.

118
10:14.640 --> 10:16.219
1…2…

119
10:22.850 --> 10:23.998
Hey, look at that.

120
10:27.442 --> 10:28.442
What?

121
10:34.014 --> 10:35.638
- More, more. - More?

122
10:54.440 --> 10:58.462
NAVINA SCHOOL

123
10:58.493 --> 11:00.470
We’re here, everybody!

124
11:00.866 --> 11:02.459
Don’t forget your bags.

125
11:02.720 --> 11:04.435
Watch your steps, guys.

126
11:04.645 --> 11:06.300
We have to go down first.

127
11:07.134 --> 11:08.134
Come on.

128
11:10.120 --> 11:11.085
Let’s go, Ji. Go, go, go.

129
11:11.120 --> 11:12.750
Come on, come on, come on.

130
11:14.168 --> 11:15.697
Come along, everyone.

131
11:16.314 --> 11:17.499
Okay, you’re all here?

132
11:17.881 --> 11:21.220
Class 7, you can take your stuff up to your rooms.

133
11:21.512 --> 11:23.401
Enjoy yourselves, everyone.

134
11:23.432 --> 11:24.742
See you at dinner.

135
11:24.790 --> 11:26.610
- Go. - Let’s go.

136
11:26.634 --> 11:28.740
Go, Ji. Let’s go.

137
11:34.628 --> 11:36.700
You guys go on a fancy trip like this every year?

138
11:36.885 --> 11:39.400
No, it’s usually a one-day trip.

139
11:39.798 --> 11:41.703
Or we go camping in the wild.

140
11:42.237 --> 11:45.097
This is the first year we get to stay at a seaside hotel.

141
11:45.374 --> 11:49.210
Actually, this hotel is part of the president’s family business,

142
11:49.490 --> 11:52.897
so we’re getting some luxurious perks this year.

143
11:53.225 --> 11:54.494
- For real? - Umm.

144
11:54.520 --> 11:56.902
Why does his family send him to a public school, then?

145
11:57.048 --> 11:59.254
Why not send him to study abroad?

146
11:59.789 --> 12:02.263
I heard he asked his dad back in middle school,

147
12:02.296 --> 12:04.097
but his dad wouldn’t let him go.

148
12:05.697 --> 12:07.462
I’ll put my things away. See you downstairs.

149
12:07.685 --> 12:08.685
See you.

150
12:10.872 --> 12:12.300
Our room is that way. Come on, Ji.

151
12:13.266 --> 12:15.230
Hurry, Ji. Change your clothes and we’ll get in the water.

152
12:15.254 --> 12:16.622
I’m still feeling car sick.

153
12:16.650 --> 12:17.952
I’ll get some rest first.

154
12:18.360 --> 12:20.303
Do you want me to stay with you?

155
12:21.830 --> 12:24.150
No, go ahead. I’m just feeling dizzy.

156
12:24.182 --> 12:25.620
Just need to lay down for a bit.

157
12:26.324 --> 12:27.383
See you later then.

158
13:12.957 --> 13:15.435
Come on. Go, go, go.

159
13:15.469 --> 13:16.469
Go back.

160
13:19.059 --> 13:20.700
What? What’s going on?

161
13:25.014 --> 13:26.400
Come on down and play with us.

162
14:24.530 --> 14:26.170
Won’t you go play in the water with them?

163
14:27.771 --> 14:29.802
No, I can’t get in the water today.

164
14:35.749 --> 14:36.802
You’re drawing again?

165
14:39.320 --> 14:42.001
You don’t get opportunities like this very often.

166
14:44.112 --> 14:48.180
Ji, do you think I’ll get into law school?

167
14:53.680 --> 14:58.160
PHAPPIM, LAWYER, IS NOT WORRIED THAT THE OPPOSING PARTY IS INFLUENTIAL. “UNDUE INFLUENCE CANNOT OVERRIDE THE LAW.”

168
14:58.200 --> 15:01.602
(Not only will you get into law school, but you’ll also be a great lawyer.)

169
15:03.862 --> 15:05.297
I know you will.

170
15:08.420 --> 15:12.198
My parents said I could do whatever I want if I get in,

171
15:13.550 --> 15:17.404
but If I get in, I’ll be busy with university exams.

172
15:17.868 --> 15:19.486
After graduation, I’ll have to take the bar exam

173
15:19.510 --> 15:20.902
and the Thai Barrister exam, too.

174
15:23.419 --> 15:25.420
Do you think I’ll have time to draw?

175
15:28.939 --> 15:30.823
Why wait until then?

176
15:34.484 --> 15:36.500
You’re going to succeed anyway.

177
15:38.565 --> 15:40.300
- You’re that sure? - Mmm.

178
15:46.445 --> 15:47.445
Thanks.

179
16:11.522 --> 16:13.702
Oh, you’re leaving?

180
16:14.183 --> 16:15.859
The sun hasn’t even set yet.

181
16:16.281 --> 16:18.703
Yeah, I’ve finished sketching.

182
16:19.248 --> 16:21.602
I’m going to color it in by the pool.

183
16:21.965 --> 16:23.499
I can enjoy the view from there.

184
16:24.005 --> 16:25.102
Besides…

185
16:27.630 --> 16:29.571
I’ll leave now. See you at dinner.

186
16:40.111 --> 16:41.150
Stay here with me.

187
16:48.974 --> 16:50.900
The president’s not joining us?

188
16:51.164 --> 16:54.300
Mr. Wira called him in to discuss the science project.

189
16:55.200 --> 16:57.899
It's been since we checked in. I wonder if they’re done yet.

190
16:58.430 --> 16:59.430
They are.

191
16:59.620 --> 17:01.970
I saw him watching the sunset with Ji by the beach.

192
17:02.000 --> 17:03.598
Oh, those two again.

193
17:04.465 --> 17:06.700
I saw them wandering around at the market, too.

194
17:07.357 --> 17:10.137
And the president always stares at Ji while he eats.

195
17:11.030 --> 17:12.099
Do you think…

196
17:12.851 --> 17:14.601
I thought that too at first.

197
17:14.973 --> 17:19.937
But when I watched them closely, it seemed like there was something more.

198
17:20.280 --> 17:23.525
Lita, did the president and Ji have some history together?

199
17:23.582 --> 17:26.660
Other than Ji hitting him in the face with a volleyball, no.

200
17:26.768 --> 17:28.099
You’ve noticed it too?

201
17:28.401 --> 17:29.401
Mmm.

202
17:29.625 --> 17:31.100
If you keep staring at someone,

203
17:31.677 --> 17:35.617
unless you’re interested in them or have a crush on them,

204
17:36.887 --> 17:38.502
there probably isn’t any other reason.

205
17:38.675 --> 17:42.896
I think he’s interested but…

206
17:43.408 --> 17:46.500
Ruth has been working harder than usual lately,

207
17:47.290 --> 17:49.349
both with the Ms. Suda situation

208
17:49.737 --> 17:53.299
and getting Ji involved in various activities.

209
17:53.565 --> 17:56.096
Hmm, maybe I’m overthinking it,

210
17:56.140 --> 17:58.699
but I feel like he’s more attached to Ji than usual.

211
18:14.030 --> 18:16.190
Would you be interested in joining the student council?

212
18:21.303 --> 18:24.779
One of our members is leaving to study elsewhere,

213
18:25.724 --> 18:28.300
so we have an opening, if you’re interested.

214
18:32.285 --> 18:34.404
No, I’ll have to pass.

215
18:37.268 --> 18:40.214
The student council organizes lots of activities.

216
18:40.970 --> 18:42.500
You’ll get to meet new people.

217
18:43.580 --> 18:46.260
Students from other grades will get to know you better too.

218
18:47.310 --> 18:48.600
You should ask someone else.

219
18:51.640 --> 18:52.699
Are you sure?

220
18:53.554 --> 18:56.416
You can take your time to think about it.

221
18:56.722 --> 18:59.001
No, don’t waste your time on me.

222
19:00.078 --> 19:03.619
There are others who are willing to do it anyway.

223
19:06.337 --> 19:09.777
Won’t you regret it if you miss this opportunity?

224
19:11.120 --> 19:13.601
No. Why would I regret it?

225
19:13.970 --> 19:15.850
It’s just not becoming a student council member.

226
19:22.925 --> 19:24.601
You wouldn’t regret it even if you died?

227
19:37.130 --> 19:38.130
No.

228
19:40.210 --> 19:42.248
There’s absolutely nothing to regret.

229
19:46.530 --> 19:47.530
What about you?

230
19:50.197 --> 19:51.197
Me?

231
19:51.580 --> 19:53.202
I looked out over the balcony

232
19:53.230 --> 19:55.130
and didn’t see you hanging out with the others.

233
19:55.162 --> 19:56.216
Where did you go?

234
19:57.134 --> 20:00.899
Oh, Mr. Wira called me in to discuss the science project.

235
20:01.269 --> 20:04.000
Then we went to talk to the hotel manager.

236
20:04.380 --> 20:06.546
- After that, we… - That’s enough.

237
20:07.971 --> 20:10.598
Did I say something wrong?

238
20:11.320 --> 20:12.320
No, it’s just…

239
20:14.045 --> 20:15.259
Don’t you ever get tired.

240
20:21.081 --> 20:22.081
Not really.

241
20:23.269 --> 20:24.697
As the class president,

242
20:25.183 --> 20:26.598
that’s what I have to do.

243
20:26.979 --> 20:27.979
Have to do?

244
20:28.491 --> 20:30.171
That means you don’t really want to do it.

245
20:30.386 --> 20:31.500
I want to.

246
20:33.598 --> 20:34.598
But…

247
20:35.582 --> 20:36.582
I…

248
20:48.468 --> 20:51.401
Why don’t you take a break from it for a while?

249
20:56.303 --> 20:58.336
I don’t mean quitting the student council,

250
20:59.334 --> 21:02.000
because I know you’re dedicated to it.

251
21:03.767 --> 21:05.539
But now you’re doing everything.

252
21:06.139 --> 21:08.305
- You’re taking on too much. - But if I stop…

253
21:10.490 --> 21:11.545
What about everyone else?

254
21:14.632 --> 21:18.139
No one would be mad at you if you were a little selfish.

255
21:19.195 --> 21:21.050
Even if someone did get mad, so what?

256
21:21.419 --> 21:22.601
Why should you care?

257
21:31.456 --> 21:34.001
You think I can just quit?

258
21:34.331 --> 21:35.604
Oh, why not?

259
21:35.736 --> 21:38.296
I thought you could step down from some of your responsibilities.

260
21:40.480 --> 21:43.177
I can, but…

261
21:59.130 --> 22:00.497
You haven’t changed at all.

262
22:12.608 --> 22:13.801
The sun has set.

263
22:14.868 --> 22:15.868
I’m sorry.

264
22:16.549 --> 22:18.303
I made you miss such a special moment.

265
22:20.170 --> 22:21.497
I wouldn’t call it missing out.

266
22:22.910 --> 22:24.097
It’s better, actually.

267
22:25.330 --> 22:26.330
What is?

268
22:27.001 --> 22:29.097
Getting to talk to you.

269
22:32.020 --> 22:33.543
Talking to you…

270
22:34.330 --> 22:37.001
makes me happier than watching the sunset.

271
22:47.630 --> 22:48.630
Ji.

272
22:48.816 --> 22:49.816
Hmm?

273
22:52.130 --> 22:53.130
Jiraphat.

274
22:59.470 --> 23:00.470
Thank you.

275
23:37.280 --> 23:39.602
Poked on the left butt, poked on the right butt

276
23:41.634 --> 23:43.977
Poked on the left butt, poked on the right butt

277
23:44.111 --> 23:46.139
Really hot, really hot, really hot!

278
24:00.208 --> 24:02.820
That was Class 1’s Cinderella performance!

279
24:02.856 --> 24:05.297
Let’s give them a round of applause!

280
24:19.840 --> 24:22.013
Class 7, gather around. Come here.

281
24:22.040 --> 24:24.318
Come on, come on.

282
24:24.358 --> 24:27.296
- When can we go back to our rooms? - Oh, stop complaining.

283
24:27.370 --> 24:31.139
When you guys see what I brought, you won’t want to get back to your rooms.

284
24:31.300 --> 24:32.899
Tada!

285
24:35.961 --> 24:37.810
Pass these around and go have fun.

286
24:37.842 --> 24:40.700
- Give these to your friends. - Okay, I’ll pass them around.

287
24:40.820 --> 24:42.146
Yeah, and be careful.

288
24:42.220 --> 24:45.500
- Remember not to leave them on the ground. - Come on, Ji. Come on, come on.

289
24:47.430 --> 24:48.430
Here.

290
24:49.382 --> 24:51.296
Oh, where’s the light?

291
24:52.130 --> 24:53.130
Hey, Kong.

292
24:56.194 --> 24:58.057
Did you sneak out to smoke again?

293
24:58.540 --> 25:00.690
Ty, that smoking thing is history.

294
25:01.000 --> 25:02.200
This is not my light.

295
25:02.346 --> 25:04.663
They all lit their sparklers so I took it.

296
25:07.140 --> 25:08.937
What? I thought you needed it.

297
25:08.962 --> 25:10.340
- Do you want it or not? - Of course.

298
25:10.377 --> 25:11.700
Light this for me, Ji.

299
25:12.075 --> 25:14.201
Do you even know how to use it?

300
25:14.630 --> 25:16.860
Of course. I used to play with these with my dad.

301
25:16.887 --> 25:18.620
Don’t worry. I got this.

302
25:19.460 --> 25:20.331
Just light it.

303
25:20.364 --> 25:21.964
If something goes wrong, I’ll handle it.

304
25:25.545 --> 25:26.614
Here I come.

305
25:26.894 --> 25:27.700
Ji!

306
25:27.770 --> 25:29.299
Woohoo woohoo!

307
25:31.877 --> 25:34.401
Kongpob, Tyler, stop fooling around.

308
25:34.539 --> 25:39.002
Cut them some slack. Let them have fun.

309
25:39.708 --> 25:41.259
I’m watching them.

310
25:41.670 --> 25:44.259
If things get out of hand, I’ll shut it down.

311
25:44.768 --> 25:45.768
Ji!

312
25:48.645 --> 25:49.645
Take this.

313
25:49.865 --> 25:50.865
You missed.

314
26:02.140 --> 26:03.140
Hey.

315
26:03.920 --> 26:05.096
Don’t you want to light it?

316
26:09.986 --> 26:11.420
If you’re scared of fire,

317
26:11.457 --> 26:13.857
I’ll light it for you and then you take it.

318
26:16.870 --> 26:18.000
(Scared of fire?)

319
26:18.669 --> 26:20.656
(Why did I say that?)

320
26:20.790 --> 26:21.790
Okay.

321
26:35.497 --> 26:36.779
The sparks aren’t hot

322
26:38.000 --> 26:40.601
but be careful of the parts that have already burned.

323
26:44.550 --> 26:45.550
Here.

324
26:52.426 --> 26:54.626
Guys, this is a nice background.

325
26:54.662 --> 26:55.897
Let me take a photo.

326
26:57.260 --> 26:59.802
- 1…2… - Mr. Tin!

327
27:01.090 --> 27:02.712
Wait for us.

328
27:02.955 --> 27:04.100
Wait for us.

329
27:04.128 --> 27:06.299
Oh, I’ve been taking pictures of you two all day.

330
27:06.342 --> 27:08.263
If you’re tired of us,

331
27:08.470 --> 27:11.645
take a picture of us with the president and Ji, then.

332
27:11.792 --> 27:14.456
Okay, okay. Let’s take a group photo.

333
27:14.576 --> 27:15.699
- Yeah. - Hold on.

334
27:15.768 --> 27:17.143
Tyler, Kongpob!

335
27:20.838 --> 27:23.626
Ji, I was wondering where you were. Here you are.

336
27:23.739 --> 27:25.740
He was hiding from you, you freak.

337
27:25.998 --> 27:27.478
But you were fooling around with me, weren’t you?

338
27:27.502 --> 27:29.656
Cut it out, guys. Let’s take a picture first.

339
27:30.430 --> 27:32.001
1…2...

340
27:32.028 --> 27:34.794
Wait for us, Mr. Tin. Don’t leave us out.

341
27:34.828 --> 27:35.828
Hey.

342
27:36.007 --> 27:38.220
This is our class’s photo. Why are you guys here?

343
27:38.522 --> 27:40.219
Hey, the president is in my class.

344
27:40.800 --> 27:42.376
- And Kongpob, too. - Mmm.

345
27:42.420 --> 27:43.754
They’re from Class 9, right?

346
27:43.786 --> 27:44.776
Come on.

347
27:44.807 --> 27:48.099
We haven’t taken a picture together since middle school.

348
27:49.641 --> 27:50.920
Hurry, Mr. Tin.

349
27:50.952 --> 27:52.697
Before too many people want to join in.

350
27:52.722 --> 27:53.374
Right.

351
27:53.617 --> 27:54.591
- Come on. - Hit it.

352
27:54.622 --> 27:55.696
Ready?

353
27:56.106 --> 27:57.700
Okay, I’ll start shooting.

354
27:57.885 --> 28:01.103
When I count to three, everyone say “Kimchi”, okay?

355
28:01.121 --> 28:01.776
- Hey? - What?

356
28:01.957 --> 28:03.780
We’re at the beach not Korea.

357
28:03.881 --> 28:04.881
Yeah.

358
28:05.469 --> 28:06.500
Say “Cheese”, then.

359
28:06.730 --> 28:09.499
- Yeah, say ‘Cheese’. - No, I don’t like cheese.

360
28:09.540 --> 28:10.265
Eh?

361
28:10.303 --> 28:11.620
But I like it.

362
28:11.651 --> 28:13.600
Okay, ready? Say “Cheese.”

363
28:13.670 --> 28:17.601
1…2…3… Cheese!

364
28:18.583 --> 28:20.202
Atiwitch, look at the camera.

365
28:20.727 --> 28:23.200
1…2…

366
28:23.499 --> 28:24.768
Cheese!

367
28:38.230 --> 28:41.402
(Jiraphat, when you grow up and have some free time, )

368
28:41.597 --> 28:43.900
(make sure to go out with the people close to you.)

369
28:47.580 --> 28:50.672
(Take lots of pictures while you still have the chance.)

370
28:54.080 --> 29:00.490
LESSONS FROM JUNE 30, 2010

371
29:19.748 --> 29:21.851
(Ask him for a picture.)

372
29:24.051 --> 29:26.060
(I heard he was drunk driving and killed someone.)

373
29:26.602 --> 29:31.103
I checked the yearbook to find the name of the man who died.

374
29:31.139 --> 29:33.496
He was a classmate of you two.

375
29:33.680 --> 29:35.160
The one I couldn’t get in touch with.

376
29:42.985 --> 29:45.402
Hey, isn’t that Ruth Atiwitch?

377
29:51.425 --> 29:55.075
(If you’re determined to take this path, don’t let me see you give up.)

378
29:55.115 --> 29:59.180
(I’ve seen your work. No matter what, you’re going to win this award.)

379
29:59.355 --> 30:02.420
(Don’t listen to that old man. (I know my son can do it.)

380
30:02.530 --> 30:05.600
(Ruth, you’re so handsome and kind.)

381
30:05.810 --> 30:08.099
(Could you spoil the ending of the drama for us?)

382
30:11.748 --> 30:15.397
Most of the people who have won this award are experienced actors.

383
30:15.600 --> 30:17.001
If you win it,

384
30:17.502 --> 30:20.179
you’ll be even more successful than your mother.

385
30:23.108 --> 30:24.299
What if I don’t want it?

386
30:36.425 --> 30:39.299
Why don’t you take a break from it for a while?

387
30:47.480 --> 30:49.930
We’re going to hang out after this event. NAWINA HOMECOMING

388
30:49.940 --> 30:51.097
Wanna join us?

389
30:51.620 --> 30:53.897
No. I have somewhere I need to be.

390
30:54.552 --> 30:55.623
Where?

391
30:56.420 --> 30:57.420
A funeral.

392
30:58.939 --> 31:00.097
Someone close to you?

393
31:00.277 --> 31:02.419
Why haven’t I heard anything about it?

394
31:03.160 --> 31:04.848
It’s an old friend who meant a lot to me.

395
31:05.930 --> 31:06.951
Old friend?

396
31:08.008 --> 31:09.902
You have friends other than me?

397
31:11.413 --> 31:13.398
How long have you known this friend?

398
31:31.920 --> 31:34.023
You should have seen Mr. Wira’s face

399
31:34.730 --> 31:37.023
when the president withdrew from the science project.

400
31:37.059 --> 31:37.990
He must have been shocked.

401
31:38.026 --> 31:40.601
Of course. Ruth is the teacher’s protégé.

402
31:41.093 --> 31:42.896
But the teacher went too far.

403
31:43.051 --> 31:45.801
He was making the president work way too hard.

404
31:46.480 --> 31:48.000
It’s a good thing he withdrew.

405
31:48.031 --> 31:49.896
Now he’ll have time to prepare for his exams.

406
31:53.309 --> 31:55.374
Mmm, this is good.

407
31:55.405 --> 31:56.445
I want some fried chicken.

408
31:56.870 --> 31:59.297
- So spicy. - Yeah, I know, right?

409
31:59.410 --> 32:01.260
I’ll pass. It doesn’t look good.

410
32:01.850 --> 32:03.456
I wasn’t gonna share. Just asking.

411
32:07.760 --> 32:09.850
GRADE 11, CLASS 7

412
32:11.011 --> 32:16.099
Ked, who’s teaching math today?

413
32:16.589 --> 32:17.589
Ms. Mai.

414
32:17.774 --> 32:20.299
Ms. Mai. But who’s Ms. Mai?

415
32:20.942 --> 32:21.942
She’s Ms. Mai.

416
32:22.248 --> 32:24.660
I heard you. But who’s the new teacher?

417
32:24.764 --> 32:25.764
Gun,

418
32:25.986 --> 32:27.377
I said, Ms. Mai.

419
32:27.488 --> 32:30.266
I know it’s the new teacher, not the old one.

420
32:30.312 --> 32:32.662
I’m not messing with you. It’s Ms. Mai.

421
32:32.693 --> 32:34.033
- You’re always messing with me. - Oh.

422
32:34.057 --> 32:35.299
I mean this new teacher.

423
32:37.248 --> 32:38.410
The teacher’s here.

424
32:41.040 --> 32:43.210
MONDAY, JULY 5, 2010

425
32:44.709 --> 32:45.709
Umm…

426
32:47.062 --> 32:49.980
Mr. Tin told me you guys were talkative.

427
32:50.013 --> 32:51.697
Why are you so quiet now?

428
32:52.480 --> 32:54.697
Attention, students.

429
32:55.909 --> 32:57.805
Good morning.

430
32:58.629 --> 32:59.805
Good morning, students.

431
33:00.222 --> 33:06.019
Starting today, I’ll be teaching math to the Arts-Languages class.

432
33:06.260 --> 33:08.131
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

433
33:08.161 --> 33:09.745
I’m Ms. Mai.

434
33:10.774 --> 33:13.952
I’ll hand out the worksheets now.

435
33:14.894 --> 33:17.197
Here, please pass them around.

436
33:27.151 --> 33:28.400
So the answer is…

437
33:29.130 --> 33:30.195
Can you tell me?

438
33:31.070 --> 33:33.530
Well done. 720.

439
33:34.210 --> 33:36.974
I’ll write down the answer for you.

440
33:37.905 --> 33:38.822
Who got it right?

441
33:38.853 --> 33:40.145
120 degrees.

442
33:40.380 --> 33:41.499
Good job.

443
33:48.158 --> 33:50.382
That’s it for today.

444
33:50.545 --> 33:51.900
See you next period.

445
33:52.180 --> 33:55.398
- Thank you. - Thank you.

446
33:57.352 --> 33:58.099
Ji.

447
33:58.271 --> 34:00.457
You asked Ji for help again?

448
34:00.755 --> 34:03.222
Will you be able to do it on your own during the actual exam?

449
34:04.222 --> 34:08.217
If you keep fooling around, you’ll be in trouble during the exam.

450
34:08.962 --> 34:11.259
Oh, Ji. Not you too.

451
34:11.413 --> 34:14.419
There’s plenty of time to study.

452
34:15.995 --> 34:17.880
Oh, Ji.

453
34:18.675 --> 34:19.979
What’s wrong with you?

454
34:20.198 --> 34:22.582
I’ve read the last question three times,

455
34:22.607 --> 34:24.820
and I still don’t understand what the poem is about.

456
34:24.859 --> 34:26.380
I’m going to fail.

457
34:26.469 --> 34:27.742
- No, you won’t. - Ahem. Ahem.

458
34:29.130 --> 34:30.299
Ty, here, buddy.

459
34:30.754 --> 34:31.754
You want one?

460
34:31.850 --> 34:32.850
What is it?

461
34:32.986 --> 34:34.016
My lucky pencil.

462
34:34.200 --> 34:36.503
It was blessed for seven days and seven nights.

463
34:38.708 --> 34:40.715
When choosing an answer, just spin it.

464
34:40.758 --> 34:42.478
Whichever number shows up, mark that answer.

465
34:42.520 --> 34:44.820
Guaranteed to help you pass! Only 10 baht each.

466
34:45.364 --> 34:47.598
- Just 10 baht? I’ll take one. - Only 10 baht.

467
34:47.940 --> 34:49.819
Next is Mr. Tin’s social studies exam.

468
34:50.350 --> 34:51.430
It’s all written questions.

469
34:51.877 --> 34:53.297
- That pencil won’t help. - Oh.

470
34:55.133 --> 34:57.020
- Thiti. - You should have studied for the exam.

471
34:57.114 --> 34:58.200
Thiti.

472
34:58.620 --> 35:00.100
You wanna get slapped, Thiti?

473
35:00.533 --> 35:01.536
Hey, easy.

474
35:01.570 --> 35:04.496
Thank you for stopping me or else he would have been dead.

475
35:05.060 --> 35:06.060
Let’s study.

476
35:07.745 --> 35:09.416
- Hey, Pim, I’ll borrow that. - Hey.

477
35:10.220 --> 35:12.004
Seems like you don’t need my pencil anymore.

478
35:13.320 --> 35:15.300
MONDAY, JULY 12

479
35:15.342 --> 35:18.297
Ji, who used our classroom? It’s so dirty.

480
35:18.437 --> 35:20.934
Look, there are pen marks and eraser shavings everywhere.

481
35:21.390 --> 35:22.502
There’s so much trash, too.

482
35:23.391 --> 35:24.602
Aren’t you going home?

483
35:24.783 --> 35:26.308
It’s not your turn to clean today.

484
35:26.345 --> 35:27.545
You don’t have to wait for me.

485
35:27.841 --> 35:29.102
Go home and study.

486
35:29.912 --> 35:33.137
It’s okay, Ji. There’s plenty of time tomorrow.

487
35:33.611 --> 35:34.699
Oh, “plenty of time.”

488
35:34.945 --> 35:36.604
You said that last time, too.

489
35:48.942 --> 35:49.942
Oh, Ji.

490
35:50.562 --> 35:52.205
I want to talk to you about something.

491
35:53.510 --> 35:54.510
What is it?

492
35:54.743 --> 35:56.955
Umm, well…

493
35:57.000 --> 35:58.000
Ji.

494
35:59.859 --> 36:01.936
Can I talk to you outside for a second?

495
36:12.210 --> 36:15.002
Here, take this. I just finished coloring it.

496
36:19.367 --> 36:20.367
Wow.

497
36:20.610 --> 36:21.610
Is it beautiful?

498
36:22.183 --> 36:24.219
It is. Why won’t you keep it?

499
36:25.788 --> 36:28.000
I was going to put it in my portfolio.

500
36:28.528 --> 36:32.201
But keeping your drawing might make it look like I have a crush on you.

501
36:33.330 --> 36:34.626
Nah, that’s cringe.

502
36:35.410 --> 36:37.900
Besides, you’re not the only one in the picture.

503
36:41.520 --> 36:43.106
See? The president’s here.

504
36:46.309 --> 36:49.625
Is that all you wanted to talk to me about?

505
36:50.176 --> 36:52.802
Oh, no. Well…

506
36:53.899 --> 36:56.201
There’s something I want to tell you before anyone else.

507
36:57.038 --> 36:58.038
Before anyone else?

508
36:58.705 --> 36:59.705
Mmm.

509
37:02.872 --> 37:05.580
I’ve decided not to apply to law school anymore.

510
37:06.060 --> 37:07.060
Huh?

511
37:07.610 --> 37:08.610
Don’t be surprised.

512
37:08.990 --> 37:11.401
I’ve decided to apply to the Faculty of Fine Arts.

513
37:11.515 --> 37:13.776
I still don’t know which major to choose,

514
37:13.810 --> 37:15.902
but I think I’ll have enough time to prepare.

515
37:16.780 --> 37:21.579
Yesterday, I just canceled my law tutoring course, and then…

516
37:24.500 --> 37:26.306
You know what the Faculty of Fine Arts is, right?

517
37:26.330 --> 37:27.897
Of course I do.

518
37:28.208 --> 37:31.200
But why did you suddenly change your mind?

519
37:32.362 --> 37:33.362
Because of you.

520
37:33.777 --> 37:34.777
Me?

521
37:34.841 --> 37:35.841
Yeah.

522
37:36.102 --> 37:38.192
You were the one who told me that

523
37:38.230 --> 37:41.002
if I wanted to draw, I should just do it instead of waiting.

524
37:41.154 --> 37:43.820
And you also told me I was definitely going to succeed.

525
37:45.583 --> 37:48.334
Everyone says artists don’t make much money

526
37:48.367 --> 37:50.334
and encourages me to study law.

527
37:50.767 --> 37:56.600
But you were the first person to praise me and support me in pursuing this path.

528
37:57.360 --> 37:58.899
That’s all I wanted to tell you.

529
37:59.549 --> 38:02.103
If you’re free, be my model again sometime.

530
38:02.820 --> 38:04.197
I’ll get going. Bye-bye.

531
38:04.905 --> 38:05.942
Get home safely, Ji.

532
38:14.290 --> 38:16.450
You guys are done talking, Ji? What’s that?

533
38:21.045 --> 38:22.045
Wow.

534
38:23.617 --> 38:24.617
Tyler,

535
38:26.060 --> 38:27.352
what did you want to tell me?

536
38:27.988 --> 38:30.417
Oh, it’s nothing important, Ji.

537
38:30.660 --> 38:33.373
At first, my dad was supposed to transfer overseas for work,

538
38:33.940 --> 38:35.220
so I was going to move with him.

539
38:36.696 --> 38:37.696
At first?

540
38:37.885 --> 38:39.696
Yeah, that was the plan.

541
38:40.583 --> 38:42.540
But now I’m not moving anymore.

542
38:44.760 --> 38:45.760
Why not?

543
38:45.893 --> 38:48.008
Mmm, because of you.

544
38:48.290 --> 38:50.356
I’ve had so much fun spending this semester with you.

545
38:50.380 --> 38:51.285
Kong, too.

546
38:51.321 --> 38:53.800
When I insisted on staying, my dad decided not to move either.

547
38:53.834 --> 38:54.939
Give me a hug.

548
38:58.285 --> 38:59.697
Why? You’re not happy?

549
38:59.730 --> 39:01.197
I’m going to throw this away.

550
39:01.340 --> 39:02.340
See you later.

551
39:09.611 --> 39:11.801
(When did everything start going wrong?)

552
39:13.134 --> 39:16.000
(I’m glad Tyler isn’t moving away.)

553
39:17.607 --> 39:20.010
(I’m glad Pim gets to do what she loves.)

554
39:21.571 --> 39:26.020
(But what if their futures fall apart because of me?)

555
39:32.008 --> 39:33.008
Oh, no!

556
39:36.760 --> 39:37.760
Ruth.

557
39:42.008 --> 39:44.000
Be careful. You’re gonna hurt yourself.

558
39:47.750 --> 39:48.750
Thank you.

559
40:09.037 --> 40:10.037
Are you okay?

560
40:11.644 --> 40:13.497
Yeah, I’m fine.

561
40:14.133 --> 40:16.499
I just missed a step.

562
40:47.208 --> 40:49.401
Oh, how’s it going?

563
40:50.020 --> 40:51.620
Are you getting used to this school yet?

564
40:52.157 --> 40:54.202
I’m still adjusting.

565
40:54.797 --> 40:57.601
Have you finished grading the exams?

566
40:58.949 --> 41:00.001
Far from it.

567
41:00.398 --> 41:03.699
Their answers are giving me a headache.

568
41:04.010 --> 41:06.500
Is grading exams really that stressful?

569
41:07.120 --> 41:08.780
You look so stressed.

570
41:09.660 --> 41:11.401
It’s not just about the exams.

571
41:13.380 --> 41:14.380
Sorry?

572
41:19.681 --> 41:22.848
(I’ve only just realized how badly my hands are shaking.)

573
41:24.000 --> 41:30.299
(It’s because I’m confused, and more than that, I’m afraid.)

574
41:31.869 --> 41:37.145
(Afraid that my very existence is ruining someone’s life and future.)

575
41:38.807 --> 41:42.660
(Does someone like me really deserve a second chance?)

576
41:54.840 --> 41:57.198
Here, drink this.

577
41:58.910 --> 41:59.998
It’ll help you calm down.

578
42:14.340 --> 42:16.874
I don’t know what you’re going through,

579
42:19.370 --> 42:21.096
but I believe everything will be okay.

580
42:26.790 --> 42:30.253
You can tell me about it when you’re ready.

581
42:34.293 --> 42:35.296
But for now…

582
42:52.644 --> 42:55.500
Just relax and take a deep breath.

583
43:33.430 --> 43:34.296
All done.

584
43:34.320 --> 43:35.320
Wow.

585
43:35.850 --> 43:36.905
It’s beautiful.

586
43:37.750 --> 43:38.750
You like it?

587
43:40.330 --> 43:41.536
I know, Ji.

588
43:42.710 --> 43:43.710
Know what?

589
43:44.081 --> 43:45.459
It’s Ruth, right?
